                "argument": "Fix \u03b8 and set T(s,t)=s\u03b8+t\u03b8\u22a5. This is an orientation-preserving orthogonal map with |det T|=1. The integrand f(T(s,t))e^{-2\u03c0i\u03c3s} is continuous and compactly supported, so Riemann-Fubini applies on a containing rectangle. Thus the one-dimensional transform of Rf is the integral over R\u00b2 of f(T(s,t))e^{-2\u03c0i\u03c3s}. Change variables x=T(s,t); since s=x\u00b7\u03b8, the result is \u222bf(x)e^{-2\u03c0i(\u03c3\u03b8)\u00b7x}dx=\\hat f(\u03c3\u03b8).",
